# Configuration for Google API Setup

# Update this file with your Google OAuth credentials information
# This is just a reference - store actual credentials in credentials.json

# Step 1: Go to Google Cloud Console (https://console.cloud.google.com/)
# Step 2: Create a new project or select existing one
# Step 3: Enable Gmail API
# Step 4: Create OAuth 2.0 Credentials (Type: Web application)
# Step 5: Download the JSON file and save it as "credentials.json" in this directory

# Authorized Redirect URIs to add in Google Cloud Console:
# - http://localhost:8080/oauth2callback
# - http://localhost:8080

# After downloading credentials.json, you're ready to run the app!
# python app.py

# Important: 
# - Never commit credentials.json to version control
# - Never share your credentials.json file
# - The app will automatically handle token storage in token.pickle
